          %h3#the_classifying_locale_functor_is_not_an_embedding The classifying locale functor is not an embedding
          %p
            It is well-known that when restricted to the subcategory
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Pro
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi FinSet
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Pro(FinSet)
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/profinite+sets"} profinite sets
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi lim
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lim
            is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fully+faithful"} fully faithful
            and in fact lands inside the subcategory of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+locales"} topological locales
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stone+spaces"} Stone spaces
          %p
            It is also true that when lifted to
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/progroups"} progroups
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi lim
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi Pro
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Grp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi Grp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Loc
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lim\colon Pro(Grp) \to Grp(Loc)
            into localic groups is fully faithful when restricted to
            %em strict
            or
            %em surjective
            progroups (those whose transition maps are surjective).
          %p
            However, in general the functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi lim
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi Pro
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Set
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi Loc
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lim\colon Pro(Set) \to Loc
            is not an embedding. For a counterexample, consider morphisms
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                    %mo →
                    %mn 2
